PLACEHOLDER — Choose a license before publishing this project.

Common options:

MIT License
  Simple and permissive. Others can use, copy, modify, and distribute
  your code freely, even in proprietary software. Just requires keeping
  your copyright notice. Good default for most open source projects.

Apache License 2.0
  Like MIT but also includes an explicit patent grant, protecting users
  from patent claims. Better for larger or more corporate projects.

GNU General Public License v3 (GPL-3.0)
  Copyleft license. Anyone who distributes your code or a modified
  version must also release their source under the GPL. Use this if
  you want to ensure derivatives stay open source.

Proprietary / All rights reserved
  No one may use, copy, or distribute your code without explicit
  permission. Use this for private or commercial projects.

Replace this file with the full license text of your chosen license.
See https://choosealicense.com for help deciding.
